r and re-style, and the result serializes to one portable spec you\ncan store and reproduce from R, Python or JavaScript.\n\n## What transfers\n\n- **Geoms and layers** — points, boxes, lines, and stats like `geom_pwc` / `stat_compare_means`.\n- **Aesthetic mappings** — `x`, `y`, `fill`, `color`, grouping.\n- **Scales, labels and facets** from the ggplot object.\n\n## When to reach for the native API instead\n\nWrapping a ggplot is ideal for reusing plots you already have. When you're building a figure fresh —\nor want fine control over CanvasXpress-specific features (clustering, dendrograms, interactive\nannotations) — call `canvasXpress()` on your data directly with a `graphType`. See the other posts\nfor that style.\n\n## Next\n\n- [Paired before/after boxplots in R](../paired-boxplots/)\n- [Interactive volcano plots in R](../volcano-plots-in-r/)\n- Gallery: <https://canvasxpress.org/examples.html>\n",
